A_435 - Although I don't actually know it... in reality I know that there are people who have perceptions or ideas about how the world around them works that I don't know and can't even imagine... a person for example with certain scientific knowledge or who he has had certain extreme sporting experiences of climbing on glaciers (just to give two examples) but he still has valuable experience and an understanding of the world. In the event that these people share their precious opinions and these are not lost, that experience becomes a &ldquo;brick&rdquo; on which to &ldquo;build&rdquo; something.